  "id": "surplus-energy-theory",
  "term": "surplus energy theory",
  "definition": "Surplus energy theory is the view, associated here with Spencer, that play happens when an organism uses up energy that has built up beyond immediate needs. On this account, play often expresses life-functions in a freer, commonly imitative form than the serious activity required under environmental pressure.",
